        "rationale": "R8/COR3 scope adaptation (KTD4): prune() gained a lease_authority parameter and a fail-closed prevalidate_reap_authority arm ahead of the graph mutation, mirroring Claude's own arm at outcome_decompose.py:282-309 (b464d090). Without it, arming leases in the worktree registry would let an authority-free prune raise WorktreeAuthorityError AFTER _commit had already mutated the spec, leaving a pruned graph pointing at an unreapable worktree. Claude moved +4/-2 across the frozen range; the Codex port is +34/-3 because Codex carries the arm plus its own prune wiring -- codex-adapt, not direct-port. CLASSIFIED RETROACTIVELY: U1 pinned five pathspecs and omitted this one, so the port landed under U5's execution with no contract row at all, and --stage classification still exited 0 because it validates the rows a contract HAS, not the ones it should have. That is the KTD8 hole this row closes. Behavior evidence is docs/validation/lease-safe-substrate-u6.json (oracles 'prune prevalidates before the graph mutation: a refused prune leaves nodes, spec_revision, registry, and lease intact' and 'prune of a lease-bound worktree without authority refuses instead of stranding the lease'), recorded against the PREDECESSOR manifest under ITS unit id U6, which maps to this plan's U5 -- the unit-id collision R4b already had to navigate.",
